# With_Mutation
This package is a follow-up of the previous package 'https://github.com/Mehrshad-Ebadi/SC-as-aGRNs' which uses the same priciples to generate artificial gene regulatory networks (aGRNs), the 
then duplicates them to model whole genome duplication (WGD).
After that, it generates four different environments and puts these aGRNs in them to measure different properties of these networks in local scale and global scale.
The main difference of this package with previous one, is that in this package I have implemented the mutation mechanism so that each node can add, remove a downstream connection of just changes the weight of that connection.
Also in this package, I have developed a new method to model self-regulation and feed-back loops as it was not possible in the previous model.

# Requirements:
1. makefile
2. C/C++ compiler (version 11 or higher preferred)
3. 8 GB of RAM for a network of 100 nodes

** for the MPI version, openmpi is required. The MPI code is written for a cluster of 13 processes. If you want to run the code on a computer with a different number of nodes, please edit the code or consider running the code on a system with at least 13 processors.


# Running the code:
in linux: To run the code, please go the directory and type 'make'. After the make process finished, the excutable file will be saved in the directory of 
./..(all versions)/Exe/Final.out

# Workflow:
1. First you need your networks to be generated and ready.

2. Then in the .txt
 
important: To run the fitness scenario, you have to copy both Results and Results_du from network generator to the fitness folder.
